# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# TOON connector node (apex) nginx config.
# Serves: relay-ws.DOMAIN  proxy.DOMAIN  faucet.DOMAIN
#
# Fixed by issue #819: this template previously pointed proxy.${DOMAIN} at
# http://connector:3000 (the retired TypeScript connector) and had no
# /health mapping, /admin guard or /rust/ guard — the live rendered
# nginx/conf.d/node.conf had already moved on to connector-rust:4000 with
# all three, so a fresh `bootstrap.sh` run from this file would have
# deployed a broken, less-hardened box. This is now a DOMAIN-parameterized
# copy of that live config's shape; see its own history there for the full
# story behind each guard below.
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

limit_req_zone $binary_remote_addr zone=node:10m rate=200r/s;

map $http_upgrade $connection_upgrade {
    default upgrade;
    ''      close;
}

map $host $backend {
    default               "";
    relay-ws.${DOMAIN}    "http://relay:7100";
    proxy.${DOMAIN}       "http://connector-rust:4000";
    faucet.${DOMAIN}      "http://faucet:3500";
}

# Full URL incl. path baked in so variable proxy_pass adds no URI. Other
# hosts fall back to their normal $backend via the empty-string default.
map $host $health_backend {
    default                              "";
    # The Rust connector has no /health route -- /ilp/identity is the
    # honest replacement: a GET that 200s only once the process is serving
    # AND has read its signer key file.
    proxy.${DOMAIN}       "http://connector-rust:4000/ilp/identity";
    faucet.${DOMAIN}      "http://faucet:3500/health";
    relay-ws.${DOMAIN}    "http://relay:3100/health";
}

server {
    listen 80;
    listen [::]:80;
    server_name relay-ws.${DOMAIN} proxy.${DOMAIN} faucet.${DOMAIN};

    location /.well-known/acme-challenge/ {
        root /var/www/certbot;
    }
    location / {
        return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
    }
}

server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    listen [::]:443 ssl;
    http2 on;
    server_name relay-ws.${DOMAIN} proxy.${DOMAIN} faucet.${DOMAIN};

    ssl_certificate     /etc/letsencrypt/live/relay-ws.${DOMAIN}/fullchain.pem;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/relay-ws.${DOMAIN}/privkey.pem;
    ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;

    resolver 127.0.0.11 valid=10s ipv6=off;

    # No anonymous connector telemetry (ADR 0008/0014, issue #665/#753) — the
    # Rust connector's operator surface is bearer-token-gated and this box
    # runs no `[operator]` section, so it exposes none at all. 404 rather
    # than 401/403 so the refusal doesn't even advertise an admin surface.
    # `^~` outranks any regex location.
    location ^~ /admin { return 404; }

    # The retired /rust/ prefix (ADR 0013, issue #601) — the parallel-fleet
    # second door to the Rust connector while TypeScript still held `/`.
    # 410, not 404 and not a redirect: a straggler hitting /rust/ilp should
    # see "permanently gone", not a connector 404 that reads like it's
    # broken, and a redirect to /ilp would silently re-point a payer's POST
    # at a route it didn't address.
    location ^~ /rust/ { return 410; }

    location = /health {
        if ($health_backend != "") {
            proxy_pass $health_backend;
        }
        if ($health_backend = "") {
            return 404;
        }
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
    }

    location / {
        if ($backend = "") { return 404; }
        limit_req zone=node burst=400 nodelay;

        proxy_pass $backend;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection $connection_upgrade;
        proxy_read_timeout 1h;

        client_max_body_size 4m;
    }
}
